      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-182573",
      ":question/problem": "Prove that $\u2211_(i = 1)^(n)(2i - 1) = n^{2}$ using mathematical induction.\n\nWe proceed using induction on $n$.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nFor the left-hand side, we have\n$2$ {{field-2}}\nwhich equals the right-hand side. Thus, our statement is {{field-3}} for $n = 1$."
